<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/027L">Corollary <span data-tag="027L">5.6.2.24</span>.</a> Let $\mathscr {F}: \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}$ be a morphism of simplicial sets and set $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}= \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F}$. Then there is a canonical isomorphism $\operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\mathscr {F}} \xrightarrow {\sim } \operatorname{hTr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}$ in the functor category $\operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}, \operatorname {h}\! \mathit{\operatorname{\mathcal{QC}}})$, which carries each vertex $C \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ to the comparison map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[ \theta _{C}: \mathscr {F}(C) \rightarrow \operatorname{hTr}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}/ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}(C) = \{ C\}  \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \int _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \mathscr {F} \]
</div>
<p> of Example <a data-tag="0272" href="/tag/0272">5.6.2.19</a>. </p>
</article>
